  "source_ref": "src_illumination_power_worksheet_20260909",
  "valid_until": {
    "date": "2036-09-24"
  },
  "validity_conditions": "This instrument, the confocal laser's 561 nm line, 4x objective, level 100%, with the worksheet's reference state: mirror in, multiband out, IR in. Worksheet Power row 89. Measured 2026-09-09 by Kyu Hwan Choi and Saksham Malik with a Thorlabs PM100A and an S120C or S121C photodiode head (which of the two is not known), the wavelength set to each line; the person confirmed on 2026-09-24 that every spot was inside the sensor, so this is the power at the sample and not a lower bound. Valid ten years from 2026-09-24 as the person stated.\n\nThe level is in `validity` as illumination_level 1 (100% written as a fraction), because it is the one condition of this measurement that is a quantity: a caller asking at another level gets a miss named, not this number. `illumination_level` is not yet a registered quantity.\n\nWHAT '100%' IS: the level setting in the acquisition software the measurement was taken with. This system cannot yet command a level -- the combiner's per-line power word is deliberately not transmitted (lunf_per_line_power_is_not_transmittable) -- so this is the output at full level, not a map from a command this system sends to an output.\n\nTHE LEVEL SWEEP, at 20x only, is partial and is not entered as linearity: rows 83-88: 0% 0, 5% '-', 10% '-', 30% 0.6, 50% 2, 100% 6.5 mW. Nothing here says the output scales with the level.\n\nNOT MEASURED: 405 nm, and 100x for any line. Nothing here extrapolates to either -- transmission does not carry across objectives, and an oil objective needs oil between lens and meter.\n\nWHAT WOULD FALSIFY IT: a change to the laser, its fibre or the light path between them and the sample; a re-measurement supersedes it.",
  "date": "2026-09-24",
  "supersedes": null,
  "conflict_with": [],
  "curated_by": "seat:librarian-20260924-1",
